[KiCad-IOS port] Round 22 build fix: define KICAD_IOS_PORT for
the pcbnew_kiface_objects, pcbcommon and 3d-viewer targets so
patches 0051/0052 actually compile in.

Diagnosis: the first round-22 CI build (run 43428316530,
SUCCESS) produced an IPA whose round22_gate FAILED: the
eeschema literal round22-fpchooser-click was present, but
every pcbnew/3d-viewer literal was absent from the shipped
binaries in every encoding, while the upstream wxLogTrace
control string from the same footprint_chooser_frame.cpp TU
was present. Root cause: this port defines KICAD_IOS_PORT
PER TARGET (patches 0026/0032/0035 and the gal/eeschema
snippets), and before this patch the define sat only on the
kicad, common, kicommon, gal and eeschema_kiface_objects
targets. Patches 0051/0052 put their #ifdef KICAD_IOS_PORT
blocks in sources compiled by three other targets --
footprint_chooser_frame.cpp (pcbnew_kiface_objects),
pcb_base_frame.cpp and tools/pcb_viewer_tools.cpp
(pcbcommon), panel_preview_3d_model.cpp and
dialog_select_3d_model.cpp (3d-viewer) -- so the blocks were
preprocessed out and the shipped build still contained the
crash. This is the exact failure mode patch 0032 documents
for rounds 10-11; the round-22 gate caught it before
delivery, which is what the gate is for.

Fix: add the define to the three targets, in the established
idiom (an iOS-only if( CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS" )
target_compile_definitions block with an inventory comment).
Safety inventory, verified against the applied tree: the
only KICAD_IOS_PORT blocks in each target's source list are
round 22's own (pcbcommon's 97 sources were checked
individually; the only hits are the two round-22 files), so
enabling the define activates nothing else.

Gate: hidden_files/round22_gate.py must now PASS on the new
build (all six literals), with the Round 21 IPA still
FAILING as negative control. The first round-22 build (md5
034bd607b8b9c8c2e11ff101aee1ad54) is NOT delivered.

Modified files:
  pcbnew/CMakeLists.txt
  common/CMakeLists.txt
  3d-viewer/CMakeLists.txt

GPL v3 section 5 notice: this file is part of the KiCad-iOS
port's modifications to KiCad 10.0.1 (commit 2db9e5a7). The
modified files carry the corresponding [KiCad-IOS port]
comments; the port is unofficial and is not affiliated with
the KiCad project. See MODIFICATIONS.md for the full change
list and the corresponding-source offer.

Apply with: patch -p1 < patches/kicad/0053-round22-define-for-pcbnew-pcbcommon-3dviewer.patch
(after patches 0001-0052)

--- a/pcbnew/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/pcbnew/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -810,6 +810,25 @@
     ${PCBNEW_SCRIPTING_SRCS}
     )
 
+# [KiCad-IOS port] Added 2026-11-13 for iOS (round 22): define
+# KICAD_IOS_PORT for the pcbnew kiface objects, the same
+# per-target define patches 0026/0032/0035 place on the kicad,
+# common, kicommon, gal and eeschema_kiface_objects targets.
+# Of the sources compiled into this target, the only
+# KICAD_IOS_PORT blocks are round 22's in
+# footprint_chooser_frame.cpp (patch 0051: the chooser's
+# skipped 3D canvas and its null guards); no other blocks
+# exist in this target's sources, so the define activates
+# nothing else. (Round 22's other patched sources compile
+# into pcbcommon and 3d-viewer, which get the same define
+# from this patch.) Without it those blocks are preprocessed
+# out of the shipped kiface -- the failure mode patch 0032
+# documents for rounds 10-11, and exactly what the first
+# round-22 build's gate caught.
+if( CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS" )
+    target_compile_definitions( pcbnew_kiface_objects PRIVATE KICAD_IOS_PORT )
+endif()
+
 if( KICAD_USE_PCH )
     target_precompile_headers( pcbnew_kiface_objects
         PRIVATE
